@startuml dict-file-format
' The two on-disk representations of a SpellingDictionary: the versioned binary
' container (feature-gated) and the always-available tab-separated text form.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/dict-file-format.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/components/dictionary/building.md, section "Persistence".
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
}
title Persistence — one lossless binary container, one lossy portable text form

rectangle "**SpellingDictionary** (in memory)\nmetadata + entries + word_index" as mem #00838F

rectangle "**words.dict** — save() / load(), feature: **serde-extras**" as bin #546E7A {
  rectangle "bytes 0..4\n**magic** = b“DICT”\nload() rejects anything else\n⇒ InvalidFormat" as b1 #1565C0
  rectangle "bytes 4..8\n**version** : u32, little-endian\nmust equal 1 ⇒ else InvalidFormat" as b2 #1565C0
  rectangle "bytes 8..EOF\n**bincode**(SpellingDictionary)\n= metadata + entries\nword_index is #[serde(skip)]" as b3 #1565C0
}

rectangle "**words.txt** — export_text() / import_text(), **always available**" as txt #546E7A {
  rectangle "the\\t1234567\nof\\t987654\nand\\t876543\n… one line per entry, in descending frequency order" as t1 #1565C0
}

rectangle "**load()** rebuilds word_index\nfrom the deserialised entries — O(V)" as reidx #455A64
rectangle "**import_text()** re-derives everything\nvia DictionaryBuilder::build_from_counts:\nN = Σ frequencies, log_prob recomputed,\nmin_frequency reset to the builder default (1)" as reimp #455A64

b1 -[hidden]right-> b2
b2 -[hidden]right-> b3

mem --> bin : save()
mem --> txt : export_text()
bin --> reidx : load()
txt --> reimp : import_text(path, language)
reidx --> mem
reimp --> mem

note right of b3
  **Round-trips exactly**: metadata (language, source,
  created_at, min_frequency, total_tokens) and every
  WordEntry, log_prob included.
end note

note right of t1
  **Lossy on purpose.** Only word and frequency survive; language,
  source, created_at and the original N are gone. Re-importing
  therefore yields a dictionary whose total_tokens is the sum of the
  **surviving** frequencies — so its log_probs are re-normalised
  and no longer agree with the exporter's.
  Lines with fewer than two tab-separated fields, or an unparsable
  count, are skipped silently.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Role |
  |<#00838F> | in-memory dictionary |
  |<#546E7A> | file on disk |
  |<#1565C0> | byte / line layout |
  |<#455A64> | reconstruction on read |
endlegend
@enduml
